From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Name HashStateBase explicitly in friend declarations

HashState and MixingHashState befriend their CRTP base through the
derived class's injected-class-name:

    friend class HashState::HashStateBase;
    friend class MixingHashState::HashStateBase;

MSVC does not resolve that in the host code nvcc 13.4 generates, so any
CUDA translation unit on Windows that includes absl/hash/hash.h fails
with

    absl/hash/internal/hash.h: error C3856: 'HashStateBase': symbol is
      not a class template

Name the base class template directly instead.  Both spellings denote
the same class, so this changes no behaviour and no ABI.

onnxruntime carries the same two-line change for the abseil it vendors:
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/blob/v1.30.0/cmake/vcpkg-ports/abseil/absl_cuda_warnings.patch

It was added there, for CUDA 13.2 and 13.3 with MSVC, in
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/pull/28736
to the patch file first created by
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/pull/27096
No abseil issue is known for it; https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/issues/2075
is a different CUDA 13 parse error.
---
diff --git a/absl/hash/hash.h b/absl/hash/hash.h
index 7a76771..2e09896 100644
--- a/absl/hash/hash.h
+++ b/absl/hash/hash.h
@@ -367,7 +367,7 @@ class HashState : public hash_internal::HashStateBase<HashState> {
  private:
   HashState() = default;
 
-  friend class HashState::HashStateBase;
+  friend class hash_internal::HashStateBase<HashState>;
   friend struct hash_internal::CombineRaw;
 
   template <typename T>
diff --git a/absl/hash/internal/hash.h b/absl/hash/internal/hash.h
index 9463746..b139397 100644
--- a/absl/hash/internal/hash.h
+++ b/absl/hash/internal/hash.h
@@ -1475,7 +1475,7 @@ class ABSL_DLL MixingHashState : public HashStateBase<MixingHashState> {
   }
 
  private:
-  friend class MixingHashState::HashStateBase;
+  friend class HashStateBase<MixingHashState>;
   template <typename H>
   friend H absl::hash_internal::hash_weakly_mixed_integer(H,
                                                           WeaklyMixedInteger);
